SUMMARY:[線上] Digital Humanities in Slavic Studies - Nataliia Laba: Pol
 itical Economy of Grief: AI-generated Media and Commercialization of War
LOCATION:
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/digital-humanities-in-slavic-studies-
 nataliialaba-political-economy-of-grief
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/digital-humanities-in-slavic-
 studies-nataliialaba-political-economy-of-grief\n\nPolitical economy of gr
 ief: AI-generated media and commercialization of war\nIf representation is
  an act of conferring visibility\, this power is now challenged by visual 
 generative AI and highly realistic synthetic images of war and conflict. S
 o far\, research on visual generative AI in the context of war and conflic
 t representation has mostly focused on the representational implications o
 f AI-generated images and their role in adding fuel to information disorde
 r. In this talk\, I shift attention to the technological infrastructures o
 f image generators and stock image sites that incentivize and at times bla
 tantly encourage curation of such images. By unpacking the relationship be
 tween the production\, representation and circulation of AI-generated imag
 es of the Russia-Ukraine war\, I discuss methodological challenges and pot
 ential solutions to studying AI-mediated commercialization and visual cons
 truction of war. \n\nBio: Nataliia Laba is an Assistant Professor in digit
 al and multimodal communication / humane AI at the University of Groningen
  in the Netherlands. She has written on AI-generated images and war repres
 entation\, sociotechnical imaginaries of visual generative AI and AGI\, an
 d visual AI style\, from critical data studies and communication perspecti
 ves. She is a co-editor of Six Critical Lenses on AI-Generated Images (CRC
  Press\, 2026). https://nataliialaba.com/ \n\nRegister for the talk over Z
 oom with Nataliia Laba
END:VEVENT
